{
  "query": "scrumtuous.com is launching a new data platform for a fast growing online marketplace and asks you to choose a managed database. The system must support both transactional processing and near real time analytics, provide low latency for reads and writes, and deliver strong consistency with replication across at least three regions for disaster recovery. Operations must remain simple with straightforward scaling and minimal administrative work. Which Google Cloud service and configuration should you select?",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Cloud Bigtable with a multi cluster routing instance and Dataflow pipelines for ETL",
      "explanation": "This pairs a wide column NoSQL database using replicated clusters with Dataflow jobs to move and transform data.",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Cloud SQL with a regional primary and read replicas together with BigQuery for analytics",
      "explanation": "This combines a managed MySQL or PostgreSQL service for OLTP workloads with BigQuery to run analytical queries.",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Cloud Spanner with a three region configuration and table interleaving",
      "explanation": "This is a distributed relational database that offers multi region consistency and supports interleaved tables for hierarchical schemas.",
      "correct": true,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "AlloyDB for PostgreSQL with cross region read replicas and BigQuery for analytics",
      "explanation": "This uses a high performance PostgreSQL compatible service with replicas in other regions and leverages BigQuery for reporting.",
      "correct": false,
