  ],
  "answer": "<p>The correct option is <b>Cloud Spanner with a three region configuration and table interleaving</b>.</p><p>This service is a fully managed relational database that provides strong consistency for reads and writes and it synchronously replicates data across multiple regions. A three region configuration delivers high availability and disaster recovery because quorum is maintained across regions, and it keeps operations simple with automatic maintenance and straightforward horizontal scaling. It supports low latency transactional workloads and can serve near real time analytical queries on the same dataset using consistent snapshots and familiar SQL.</p><p>Table interleaving in this service co locates related parent and child rows which improves locality for joins and common access patterns. This reduces latency for both transactional access and operational analytics while keeping the schema and operations simple.</p><p><i>Cloud Bigtable with a multi cluster routing instance and Dataflow pipelines for ETL</i> does not meet the transactional and consistency requirements. It lacks multi row transactions and cross cluster replication is eventually consistent, and building analytics through pipelines adds operational complexity rather than simplifying it.</p><p><i>Cloud SQL with a regional primary and read replicas together with BigQuery for analytics</i> uses asynchronous replicas across regions, so it cannot provide strong consistency for reads in multiple regions. Scaling is mostly vertical and managing data movement into BigQuery adds administrative work, and there is still only a single write region.</p><p><i>AlloyDB for PostgreSQL with cross region read replicas and BigQuery for analytics</i> offers high performance and Postgres compatibility, but cross region replicas are asynchronous and there is only one write region. This fails the requirement for strong consistency with replication across at least three regions and it also adds an extra analytics stack to operate.</p>",
