  "originalQuery": "You are a Database Engineer tasked with designing a cloud database solution for a rapidly growing e-commerce company. The database must be able to handle a mix of transactional and analytical workloads, provide low-latency reads and writes, and support strong consistency with multi-region replication for disaster recovery. Additionally, the database must be easy to manage, scale, and maintain. Which of the following Google Cloud Platform services and configurations would best meet these requirements?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Cloud Bigtable with instance clustering and Dataflow for ETL tasks<br/>B. Cloud Spanner with multi-region instance and interleaved tables<br/>C. Cloud SQL with regional instances and read replicas, combined with BigQuery for analytical workloads<br/>D. Cloud Datastore with multi-region instances, combined with BigQuery for analytical workloads",
